{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016vKyRwqHBHaBQALUX3upR6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full PDF and the review context YAML. Let me summarize what I know:\n\n**Paper**: \"When Do Self-Extracted Symbolic Constraints Help LLM Reasoning? A Diagnostic Study\"\n\n**Core idea**: SICA (Symbolic Invariant Consensus Aggregation) extracts FOL constraints from LLM reasoning traces and uses MAX-SAT to aggregate them. The paper is a diagnostic study asking when this helps over simple self-consistency (SC).\n\n**Key findings**:\n1. Oracle gap: Gold FOL constraints yield +14.2pp over SC, proving the mechanism works\n\n\n2. Self-extracted constraints backfire in most conditions, with only one marginal positive result on Mistral-7B that doesn't hold consistently across seeds\n3. Nine attempted fixes all fail to bridge the gap between what's theoretically possible and what actually works in practice\n4. The review feedback suggests reframing away from the Condorcet framework toward a pure diagnostic lens, though some unexpected results like multi-temperature improvements complicate the failure narrative\n\nNow I'm setting up two parallel reviewers—one focused on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and positioning—then running them through a structured roundtable where they first evaluate independently, share findings, identify convergences, and synthesize a coherent assessment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15645,"cache_read_input_tokens":36743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15645},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff4131df-0538-40e9-a5d8-d0234a1df865","uuid":"053fb0e1-5ca1-4465-b773-2dc665942ef7"}
