{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W2jq5xTb3UKok6vxmEH3w7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\begin{abstract}\n2\tNeuro-symbolic methods extract first-order logic (FOL) constraints from Large Language Model (LLM) reasoning traces to improve answer aggregation beyond majority voting. Whether the reasoning model itself can produce useful constraints through self-extraction remains an open question. We evaluate Symbolic Invariant Consensus Aggregation (SICA), which formulates a weighted partial Maximum Satisfiability (MAX-SAT) problem over self-extracted FOL constraints, across seven models from four base architectures (7B to 32B parameters) on four reasoning domains with more than 2,400 total instances. SICA benefits exist only in a narrow Goldilocks zone ($\\sim$50--55\\% Self-Consistency): Mistral-7B achieves $+4.90$ percentage points on FOLIO ($p = 0.013$). Outside this band, SICA fails in three distinct ways. Above $\\sim$60\\% Self-Consistency, confirmation bias causes constraints to mirror model answers, reducing SICA to majority voting (eight conditions, all nonsignificant). Below $\\sim$40\\%, predominantly incorrect traces produce noisy constraints that actively hurt performance (Mistral-7B on ProofWriter-D5: $\\Delta = -4.67$ pp). When domain structure resists formalization, extraction yields no discriminative signal regardless of accuracy. Oracle controls substituting gold FOL annotations yield $+14.22$ and $+11.50$ percentage points (both $p < 0.001$), confirming that aggregation works with discriminative constraints and localizing the bottleneck to extraction quality. Six remediation strategies, including in-context learning with gold FOL examples, all fail to widen this zone. The multi-candidate rate $C_0$ combined with Self-Consistency accuracy provides a two-dimensional deployment diagnostic.\n3\t\\end{abstract}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016Hb6xFUswTjtRS1U7uZuVP","session_id":"ff4131df-0538-40e9-a5d8-d0234a1df865","uuid":"ae41ffca-8538-4cf5-884b-50f93a3c8f85","timestamp":"2026-05-19T04:49:36.881Z"}
