{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GP3F3KZXtMGhyoKuAkTDvM","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_3/projects/symb_invariant_consensus/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Writing Plan — symb_invariant_consensus\\\\n# Generated: 2026-05-19T14:00:00Z\\\\n# Updated: 2026-05-19T16:00:00Z — D060: Method improvement failed → pure analysis paper\\\\n# Full Draft: Independence Bottleneck (Condorcet) — Analysis paper\\\\n# Paper Agent Step 1 output\\\\n\\\\nmeta:\\\\n  venue: EMNLP 2026\\\\n  track: main\\\\n  template: templates/latex/acl/\\\\n  template_note: \\\\\\\"ACL template shared by EMNLP; confirm 2026 style options when official EMNLP 2026 CFP releases\\\\\\\"\\\\n  page_limit: 8\\\\n  deadline: 2026-05-25\\\\n  title: >\\\\n    Beyond Self-Consistency: How Trace Independence Limits\\\\n    Symbolic Consensus in LLM Reasoning\\\\n  core_claim: >\\\\n    Self-consistency's theoretical basis (Condorcet Jury Theorem) requires voter\\\\n    independence, but same-model sampling severely violates this assumption\\\\n    (Fleiss' κ = 0.21–0.82, Effective-K only 1.20–3.63 for nominal K=12). Oracle control\\\\n    (+14.22pp) proves the aggregation mechanism works, but self-extracted\\\\n    constraints capture only 35% of this ceiling. Nine remediation strategies\\\\n    spanning prompting, architecture, capability, verification, diversity, and\\\\n    filtering dimensions all fail, confirming the independence bottleneck is\\\\n    structural.\\\\n  paper_type: \\\\\\\"Analysis paper (Condorcet theoretical framework + empirical diagnosis + 9 remediation failures)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  framing: \\\\\\\"Independence Bottleneck (Condorcet)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  d060_note: \\\\\\\"Method improvement (multi-temp, filtering, T=1.0) all failed → pure analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n  created_at: 2026-05-19T14:00:00Z\\\\n  updated_at: 2026-05-19T16:00:00Z\\\\n\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n# Contributions (4 verified)\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\ncontributions:\\\\n  - id: C1\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"Independence Bottleneck\\\\\\\"\\\\n    status: VERIFIED\\\\n    claim: >\\\\n      Condorcet Jury Theorem requires voter independence; same-model traces\\\\n      violate this (Mistral κ=0.50 Eff-K=1.85 [hero], Qwen κ=0.744 Eff-K=1.31).\\\\n      Range: κ=0.21–0.82, Eff-K=1.20–3.63. exp-046 has highest Eff-K (3.63)\\\\n      but SC too low (39%) → negative Δ. Cross-seed κ varies (0.50/0.41/0.40)\\\\n      but Δ non-monotonic with Eff-K → Eff-K is necessary but not sufficient.\\\\n    evidence: \\\\\\\"§5.1, Table 3, Figure 3\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: C2\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"Oracle Gap — Extraction Bottleneck\\\\\\\"\\\\n    status: VERIFIED\\\\n    claim: >\\\\n      Gold FOL + MAX-SAT = +14.22pp (p=2.0e-7) FOLIO, +11.50pp PW. Self-extraction\\\\n      captures only 35% of oracle ceiling. Aggregation mechanism sound; extraction\\\\n      quality is the binding bottleneck.\\\\n    evidence: \\\\\\\"§4.3, Table 1 (oracle rows)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: C3\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"Regime-Dependent Capability Trap\\\\\\\"\\\\n    status: VERIFIED\\\\n    claim: >\\\\n      SICA effectiveness depends on model accuracy regime: Type A (SC≥~60%,\\\\n      confirmation bias), Type B (non-formalizable domain), Type C (SC≤~40%,\\\\n      noisy constraints, Δ=-2.83pp p=0.0095). Goldilocks zone (~50–55% SC)\\\\n      yields only significant gain (+4.90pp, p=0.013, 2/3 seeds significant at α=0.05).\\\\n    evidence: \\\\\\\"§4.2, §4.4, §4.5, Table 1, Figure 2\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: C4\\\\n    label: \\\\\\\"C0+SC Deployment Diagnostic + K/T Sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    status: VERIFIED\\\\n    claim: >\\\\n      C0 (multi-candidate rate) + SC accuracy forms zero-cost deployment diagnostic.\\\\n      K sensitivity shows inverted-U (K=12 sweet spot). T sensitivity shows effect\\\\n      fragility (T=0.7 +4.90pp → T=1.0 +0.55pp). Nine remediation strategies\\\\n      spanning all intervention dimensions fail, confirming structural bottleneck.\\\\n    evidence: \\\\\\\"§5.3, §5.4, §5.5, Figure 3, Appendix remediation table\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n# Paper Outline\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\npaper_outline:\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    file: abstract.tex\\\\n    word_budget: 220\\\\n    phase: 2\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem: SC (majority voting) plateaus; Condorcet Jury Theorem explains why — traces lack independence\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Method: SICA pipeline, 7 models (7B–32B), 4 domains, N>2,400\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Independence quantification: Fleiss' κ=0.21–0.82 → Eff-K=1.20–3.63 at K=12\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Regime-dependent effect: +4.90pp Goldilocks zone (2/3 seeds significant), -2.83pp Type C, ~0 Type A\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Oracle +14.22pp/+11.50pp proves aggregation sound\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"9 remediation strategies all fail — bottleneck is structural\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"K sensitivity: inverted-U (K=12 sweet spot); T sensitivity: fragile (T=0.7→T=1.0 collapses)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"C0+SC deployment diagnostic\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, analysis, method]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    file: introduction.tex\\\\n    word_budget: 1300\\\\n    phase: 2\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"P1: Scaling test-time computation; SC as dominant aggregation; diminishing returns (Loo et al. 2025)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"P2: Neuro-symbolic methods (Logic-LM, LINC, DyLoS, Aristotle, FoVer) show gains but use external/trained components. Can same-model self-extraction suffice?\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"P3: Theoretical lens — Condorcet Jury Theorem requires voter independence. Same-model traces violate this (Eff-K=1.20–3.63). Symbolic verification could inject independent signal, but self-extraction inherits trace non-independence.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"P4: Our approach — SICA pipeline + Condorcet analysis + 7 models × 4 domains + 3-seed replication. Core finding: independence bottleneck. 9 remediation strategies all fail.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"P5: Contributions (C1–C4)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, analysis, method]\\\\n    figures: [fig1_pipeline]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    file: related_work.tex\\\\n    word_budget: 800\\\\n    phase: 1\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 1: SC and extensions — SC, USC, weighted SC, DiVeRSe, scaling plateaus\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 2: Neuro-symbolic reasoning — Logic-LM, LINC, DyLoS, Aristotle, FoVer, LogicAgent; key distinction: trained/external vs same-model self-extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 3: Test-time compute — Snell et al. 2025, DeepSeek-R1, diversity-aware TTS\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 4: Verification and reranking — ORM, PRM, Math-Shepherd\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 5: Condorcet/voting theory and ensemble diversity — Condorcet 1785, Austen-Smith & Banks 1996, arXiv:2409.00094 (closest prior work)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: method\\\\n    file: method.tex\\\\n    word_budget: 1200\\\\n    phase: 1\\\\n    subsections:\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:condorcet\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Self-Consistency and the Condorcet Independence Assumption\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 300\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"SC as majority voting; Condorcet Jury Theorem: K independent voters with p>0.5 → correct majority as K→∞\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"LLM traces violate independence: same model, same prompt, only sampling temperature\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Eff-K = K / (1 + (K-1)·κ) where κ = Fleiss' Kappa — effective independent voter count\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"When Eff-K ≈ 1, additional traces provide no new information\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:sica-pipeline\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"SICA Pipeline\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 450\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"K-trace generation at T=0.7\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"FOL constraint extraction at T_ext=0.3 (in practice: predominantly ground propositional clauses)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Syntactic deduplication\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Weighted partial MAX-SAT: hard clauses (answer assertion), soft clauses (constraints weighted by occurrence)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Z3 solver, 10s timeout per candidate; answer with highest satisfiable subset selected\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:oracle-design\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Oracle Control Design\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 200\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Replace self-extracted constraints with gold FOL (FOLIO) / DSL (ProofWriter)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Z3 evaluates gold constraint against each candidate answer\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Causal intervention: isolates constraint quality from aggregation mechanism\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:scope\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Scope\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 100\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Same-model self-extraction pipeline\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Methods using trained extractors / external provers out of scope\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    figures: [fig1_pipeline]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experiments\\\\n    file: experiments.tex\\\\n    word_budget: 1800\\\\n    phase: 1\\\\n    subsections:\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:exp-setup\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Experimental Setup\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 300\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"7 models: Qwen2.5-14B, Qwen2.5-7B, Qwen3-14B, Mistral-7B-v0.3, LLaMA-3.1-8B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B, QwQ-32B\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"4 domains: FOLIO (n=204), ProofWriter (n=600), LogiQA (n=200), StrategyQA (n=200/60)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Probes: GSM8K (n=30), AIME 2024 (n=22)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"K=12, T=0.7, T_ext=0.3, Z3 timeout 10s\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Metrics: accuracy (%), Δ=SICA−SC (pp), McNemar exact test α=0.05, 95% bootstrap CIs\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:main-results\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Main Results: A Regime-Dependent Effect\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 450\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Table 1: all conditions sorted by SC%, grouped by regime\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Goldilocks zone (~50–55% SC): Mistral FOLIO +4.90pp p=0.013 (b=12,c=2)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Type A (SC≥~60%): 8+ conditions, all n.s., combined N>2,000\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Type C (SC≤~40%): Mistral PW-600 Δ=-2.83pp p=0.0095 — SICA hurts\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Degenerate: C0<5% (QwQ, GSM8K) → SICA≡SC\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-033, exp-046, exp-041, exp-026, exp-035, exp-038, exp-020, exp-027, exp-019, exp-044b, exp-050b, exp-049b, exp-014, exp-017, exp-012, sica_aime30_v3\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:oracle\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Oracle Control: Aggregation Is Sound\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 300\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"FOLIO: oracle-SICA 89.71% vs SC 75.49% (+14.22pp, p=2.0e-7, b=29, c=0)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"ProofWriter: oracle-SICA 86.67% vs SC 75.17% (+11.50pp, p=9.21e-15)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Z3 gold agreement: 95.1% FOLIO, 97.1% PW\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Best self-extraction captures 34.5% of oracle ceiling\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-031, exp-022\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:replication\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Three-Seed Replication\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 250\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Mistral-7B FOLIO-204: seeds 42/123/456\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Seed 42 (exp-033): Δ=+4.90pp p=0.013\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Seed 123 (exp-052): Δ=+3.43pp p=0.039\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Seed 456 (exp-053): Δ=-0.49pp p=1.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"2/3 seeds significant at α=0.05; mean Δ=+2.61pp\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Variance across seeds highlights sensitivity to sampling → motivates independence analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-033, exp-052, exp-053\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:failure-modes\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Failure Mode Analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 300\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Type A: strong models → consistent traces → constraints mirror answers → MAX-SAT = counting\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Type B: non-formalizable domain (LogiQA: extraction rate 86.4%, contradiction rate 0.8%)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Type C: wrong traces → wrong constraints → solver amplifies errors\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    tables: [tab1_main_results]\\\\n    figures: [fig2_regime_scatter]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: analysis\\\\n    file: analysis.tex\\\\n    word_budget: 1500\\\\n    phase: 1\\\\n    subsections:\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:effective-k\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Condorcet Effective-K Analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 350\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Fleiss' κ per model-domain condition from K=12 trace answer distributions\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Eff-K = K / (1 + (K-1)·κ)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Mistral FOLIO s42: κ=0.500, Eff-K=1.85 (hero); s123: κ=0.412, Eff-K=2.17; s456: κ=0.401, Eff-K=2.22\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Mistral PW-600: κ=0.210, Eff-K=3.63 (highest Eff-K but SC=39% → negative Δ)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Qwen-14B FOLIO: κ=0.744, Eff-K=1.31 (most redundant)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Qwen-14B LogiQA: κ=0.821, Eff-K=1.20 (lowest Eff-K)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Cross-seed κ varies (0.50/0.41/0.40) but Δ non-monotonic with Eff-K → Eff-K necessary not sufficient; need both Eff-K AND SC in operating range\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Correlation: higher Eff-K → more room for SICA gain\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Explains SC plateau: adding traces beyond Eff-K provides no new information\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"comp-1 Worker output (Fleiss' κ from per-problem trace data)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:extraction-taxonomy\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Extraction Error Taxonomy\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 250\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Discriminative rate: ~8% Z3-discriminative (95% CI [7.6, 8.8])\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Even removing non-discriminative constraints provides zero gain (filtering experiment)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Variable naming inconsistency: 56.4% constraint pairs share zero Z3 variables\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Self-extraction captures ~18% of oracle quality\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-023, exp-036b; filtering validation data\\\\\\\"\\\\n        note: \\\\\\\"D060: 43.1% trivially_satisfied number under review — use verified ~8% non-discriminative framing\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:k-sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"K Sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 250\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Inverted-U curve: K=4 Δ=-1.47pp, K=8 Δ=-0.98pp, K=12 Δ=+4.90pp, K=16 Δ=+1.47pp\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"K=12 is sweet spot; K=4 SC ≈ K=12 SC but SICA differs by ~6.4pp\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Proves SICA extracts different information than SC at sufficient K\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Links to Eff-K: diminishing returns from non-independent traces\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"K=20 pending\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"Director K sensitivity data; registry: exp-051\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:t-sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Temperature Sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 100\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"T=0.7: Δ=+4.90pp (exp-033); T=1.0: Δ=+0.55pp (exp-054)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Effect extremely fragile to temperature — higher T increases diversity but degrades trace quality\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-033, exp-054\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:entropy\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Entropy-Conditioned Mechanism\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 200\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Per-problem answer entropy mediates SICA effectiveness\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Mistral: low Δ=0, med Δ=+4.5, high Δ=+9.6pp (monotonic)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Proportion of high-entropy problems: Mistral 35.8% vs Qwen 10.3%\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Causal chain: strong model → consistent traces → low entropy → redundant constraints\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-033 per_entropy, exp-026\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:ablation\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Constraint Ablation\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 100\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"MAX-SAT vs count-only: 803/804 agree (Qwen-14B, n=804)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"Self-extracted constraints carry no signal beyond vote counts in high-SC regime\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: sica_constraint_ablation_013\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - id: \\\\\\\"sec:remediation\\\\\\\"\\\\n        title: \\\\\\\"Remediation Analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n        word_budget: 250\\\\n        bullets:\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"9 strategies spanning 6 intervention dimensions, all fail:\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"  Prompting: contrastive extraction (exp-029: disc_rate 8.2%→6.0%, Δ=-1.1pp)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"  Architecture: cross-model extraction (exp-030: 0% discriminative)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"  Capability: generational scaling Qwen3 (exp-027: +0.49pp n.s.)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"  Verification: Z3 feedback (exp-036: 0.9% UNSAT trigger), cross-trace UNSAT (exp-036b: 56.4% zero vars)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"  Diversity: multi-temp sampling (n=28, Δ=0.00pp), T=1.0 (Δ=+0.55pp, collapse from +4.90pp)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"  Filtering: discriminative constraint filtering (0 gain)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"  Consistency: consistency filtering (exp-043: reverts to SC at T≥4)\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"All fail → independence bottleneck is structural, not addressable by prompt/solver/diversity interventions\\\\\\\"\\\\n          - \\\\\\\"1-paragraph summary in main text; full table in appendix\\\\\\\"\\\\n        data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-029, exp-030, exp-027, exp-036, exp-043, exp-036b; D060 new data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    tables: [tab3_independence, tab4_extraction_taxonomy]\\\\n    figures: [fig3_k_sensitivity]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: discussion\\\\n    file: discussion.tex\\\\n    word_budget: 500\\\\n    phase: 2\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Oracle causally isolates bottleneck: aggregation sound, extraction binding\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Condorcet interpretation: Eff-K < 2 → constraints inherit trace non-independence\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"9 remediation failures confirm structural nature — not addressable by prompting, architecture, diversity, or filtering\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Why published methods (DyLoS, Aristotle, FoVer) succeed: bypass same-model self-extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"exp-050b complication: ICL changes trace generation characteristics, not just SC level\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"C0 × SC two-dimensional deployment diagnostic\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Paths forward: trained extractors, external provers, multi-model pipelines\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, analysis]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: conclusion\\\\n    file: conclusion.tex\\\\n    word_budget: 300\\\\n    phase: 2\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SICA evaluated: 7 models (7B–32B), 4 domains, N>2,400, 3-seed replication\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Independence bottleneck: Eff-K=1.20–3.63 limits both SC and SICA\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Regime-dependent: Goldilocks zone (+4.90pp, 2/3 seeds significant), Type C hurts (-2.83pp), Type A n.s.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Oracle +14.22pp/+11.50pp proves aggregation; 9 remediation strategies all fail\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"K=12 sweet spot (inverted-U); T=0.7→T=1.0 collapses effect\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"C0 + SC as deployment diagnostic\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, analysis]\\\\n\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n# Visualization Plan\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nvisualization_plan:\\\\n  - fig_id: fig1_pipeline\\\\n    type: conceptual\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      SICA pipeline diagram: K traces → FOL constraint extraction →\\\\n      syntactic deduplication → weighted partial MAX-SAT (Z3) → answer selection.\\\\n      Include oracle branch. Annotate independence bottleneck at extraction stage.\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"Pipeline architecture and where independence bottleneck manifests\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes: >\\\\n      Update existing TikZ pipeline. Add \\\\\\\"Independence Bottleneck\\\\\\\" annotation.\\\\n      No SICA+ components (D060: method improvement removed).\\\\n    placement: method\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"16:6\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual (existing TikZ code)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    status: \\\\\\\"EXISTS — minor label update\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig2_regime_scatter\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      SC accuracy (x) vs SICA Δpp (y) scatter. All model-domain conditions.\\\\n      3 replication seeds as separate points. Color by significance.\\\\n      Regime zone annotations (Type A/C, Goldilocks).\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"Hero figure: regime-dependent SICA effectiveness\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes: >\\\\n      Solid markers n≥100, hollow n<100. Horizontal Δ=0 line.\\\\n      Green band ~50–55% SC. Use exp-046 FINAL (n=600, SC=39.33%, Δ=-2.83pp).\\\\n      Three Mistral seeds at SC≈54–56%. Width 0.75\\\\\\\\textwidth.\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: >\\\\n      registry: exp-033, exp-052, exp-053, exp-046, exp-041, exp-026,\\\\n      exp-035, exp-038, exp-020, exp-027, exp-019, exp-044b, exp-050b,\\\\n      exp-049b, exp-014, exp-017, exp-012, sica_aime30_v3\\\\n    status: \\\\\\\"UPDATE — add 3 seeds + exp-046 FINAL\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig3_k_sensitivity\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      Two-panel figure. (a) K vs SICA Δpp showing inverted-U curve:\\\\n      K=4(-1.47), K=8(-0.98), K=12(+4.90), K=16(+1.47).\\\\n      (b) Actual K vs Eff-K bar chart per model showing independence deficit.\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"K=12 is sweet spot; inverted-U reveals interaction between diversity and constraint quality\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes: >\\\\n      Panel (a): line plot with markers and error bars if available.\\\\n      Panel (b): grouped bars — actual K (gray) vs Eff-K (colored per model).\\\\n      Subfigure layout. Width 0.75\\\\\\\\textwidth.\\\\n    placement: analysis\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"2:1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"Director K sensitivity data + comp-1 Eff-K computation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    status: \\\\\\\"NEW — requires comp-1 output for panel (b)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n# Table Plan\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\ntable_plan:\\\\n  - table_id: tab1_main_results\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    width: \\\\\\\"table*\\\\\\\"\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"SICA vs SC across all conditions, sorted by SC accuracy. Includes 3-seed replication and oracle upper bounds.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    columns: [Model, Domain, n, \\\\\\\"SC (%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SICA (%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Δ (pp)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"p\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: >\\\\n      registry: exp-033, exp-052, exp-053, exp-046 (FINAL: n=600 SC=39.33\\\\n      Δ=-2.83 p=0.0095), exp-041, exp-026/sica_expanded_14b, exp-035,\\\\n      exp-038, exp-020, exp-027, exp-019, exp-044b, exp-014, exp-017,\\\\n      exp-012, sica_aime30_v3, exp-031, exp-022\\\\n    notes: >\\\\n      Grouped by regime: Type C, Goldilocks (with 3 seeds), Type A, Degenerate, Oracle.\\\\n      Merge replication + oracle into single table. Use exp-046 FINAL numbers.\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab3_independence\\\\n    type: analysis\\\\n    placement: analysis\\\\n    width: \\\\\\\"table\\\\\\\"\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Condorcet independence analysis by model-domain condition.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    columns: [Model, Domain, \\\\\\\"Fleiss' κ\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Eff-K\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Unanimous (%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Confirm. bias (%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SICA Δ (pp)\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"comp-1 Worker output + registry metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"C1 contribution table. Requires comp-1 computation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab4_extraction_taxonomy\\\\n    type: analysis\\\\n    placement: analysis\\\\n    width: \\\\\\\"table\\\\\\\"\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Extraction quality: constraint discriminativeness and variable sharing.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    columns: [Metric, Value, Description]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-023, exp-036b\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"~8% Z3-discriminative, 56.4% zero shared vars, filtering = 0 gain\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  # Appendix tables\\\\n  - table_id: tab_app_remediation\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Nine remediation strategies targeting the independence bottleneck.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    columns: [Strategy, Dimension, \\\\\\\"Key metric\\\\\\\", Result]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry + D060 data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Original 6 + filtering + T=1.0 + multi-temp. All fail.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_app_entropy\\\\n    type: analysis\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"SICA Δ by answer entropy bin.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-033, exp-026 per_entropy\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_app_oracle_subtype\\\\n    type: detail\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Oracle-SICA by ProofWriter subtype.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-022\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_app_k_ablation\\\\n    type: detail\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"K sensitivity detailed: SICA Δ, SC accuracy, and diversity metrics by K.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"Director K sensitivity data; registry: exp-051, sica_k_sensitivity_14b\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_app_replication\\\\n    type: detail\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Seed replication detailed analysis.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-033, exp-052, exp-053\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n# Literature Strategy\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nliterature_strategy:\\\\n  citation_budget: 40\\\\n  micro_clusters:\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"self_consistency_and_variants\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Wang et al. 2023 (Self-Consistency)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Chen et al. 2023 (USC)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Loo et al. 2025 (SC scaling re-evaluation)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Taubenfeld et al. 2025 (confidence-weighted SC)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"self-consistency majority voting LLM reasoning 2023 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"DiVeRSe diverse verifier reasoning steps\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"symbolic_reasoning_llm\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 8\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Pan et al. 2023 (Logic-LM)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Olausson et al. 2023 (LINC)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Xu et al. 2026 (DyLoS)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Li et al. 2025 (Aristotle)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Wang et al. 2025 (FoVer)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Luo et al. 2025 (LogicAgent)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"neuro-symbolic reasoning LLM formal logic solver 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"test_time_compute_scaling\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Snell et al. 2025 (scaling test-time compute, ICLR Oral)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Guo et al. 2025 (DeepSeek-R1)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"test-time compute scaling LLM reasoning 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"verification_reranking\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Cobbe et al. 2021 (ORM / GSM8K)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Lightman et al. 2023 (PRM)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"outcome reward model process reward model verification 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"condorcet_voting_theory\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Condorcet 1785 (Jury Theorem)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Austen-Smith & Banks 1996 (information aggregation)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"arXiv:2409.00094 (closest prior work — Condorcet applied to LLM aggregation)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Condorcet jury theorem machine learning ensemble diversity\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"effective ensemble size correlated voters independence\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Fleiss kappa inter-rater agreement reliability\\\\\\\"\\\\n      notes: \\\\\\\"Must verify arXiv:2409.00094 content and cite appropriately\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"constraint_satisfaction_nlp\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 3\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"de Moura & Bjorner 2008 (Z3)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SAT solver NLP constraint satisfaction 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"self_correction_negative\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 3\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Huang et al. 2024 (LLMs cannot self-correct reasoning)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LLM self-correction reasoning limitations 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"benchmarks\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Han et al. 2022 (FOLIO)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Tafjord et al. 2021 (ProofWriter)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Liu et al. 2020 (LogiQA)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Geva et al. 2021 (StrategyQA)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Cobbe et al. 2021 (GSM8K)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"debate_multi_agent\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 3\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Liang et al. 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Du et al. 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LLM debate multi-agent reasoning aggregation 2023 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"compositionality\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 1\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Press et al. 2023 (compositionality gap)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n# Writing Order\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  - method          # Phase 1: Condorcet + SICA pipeline + Oracle design\\\\n  - experiments     # Phase 1: data-driven, Table 1 hero\\\\n  - analysis        # Phase 1: Eff-K + taxonomy + K/T sensitivity + entropy + remediation\\\\n  - related_work    # Phase 1: standalone\\\\n  - introduction    # Phase 2: depends on all above\\\\n  - discussion      # Phase 2: depends on all empirical\\\\n  - abstract        # Phase 2: last\\\\n  - conclusion      # Phase 2: last\\\\n\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n# Page Budget\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\npage_budget:\\\\n  target: 8.0\\\\n  breakdown:\\\\n    abstract: 0.3\\\\n    introduction: 1.3\\\\n    related_work: 0.8\\\\n    method: 1.2\\\\n    experiments: 1.8\\\\n    analysis: 1.5\\\\n    discussion: 0.5\\\\n    conclusion: 0.3\\\\n    total_text: 7.7\\\\n    figures_tables_float: 0.3\\\\n  compression_notes:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"Oracle can merge into tab1 (save separate table float)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"Replication as 3 rows in tab1 (no separate table)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"Remediation: 1 paragraph main text + full table in appendix\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"Entropy: compact paragraph, move detailed table to appendix\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"No SICA+ sections (D060: method removed) — frees ~0.5pp for deeper analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n# Pre-requisite Computations\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nrequired_computations:\\\\n  - id: comp-1\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"Fleiss' Kappa + Effective-K\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      Compute Fleiss' κ from per-problem trace answer distributions for all\\\\n      model-domain conditions. Director-provided values: Mistral κ=0.501\\\\n      (Eff-K=1.82), Qwen κ=0.739 (Eff-K=1.31). Verify and compute for\\\\n      remaining conditions.\\\\n    priority: HIGH\\\\n    blocking: [fig3_k_sensitivity, tab3_independence, \\\\\\\"§5.1\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    status: \\\\\\\"DONE — comp-1 Worker verified; exp-033 κ pending (westd-25068 inaccessible)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: comp-2\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"Extraction taxonomy verification\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      D060 update: 43.1% trivially_satisfied number under review. Filtering\\\\n      experiment found ~8% non-discriminative. Use verified ~8% Z3-discriminative\\\\n      framing. Verify exact taxonomy breakdown from exp-023 data.\\\\n    priority: MEDIUM\\\\n    blocking: [tab4_extraction_taxonomy, \\\\\\\"§5.2\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n# Key Data (truth source: registry)\\\\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\nkey_data:\\\\n  hero_result:\\\\n    exp_id: exp-033\\\\n    model: Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3\\\\n    dataset: FOLIO-204\\\\n    sc: 54.41\\\\n    sica: 59.31\\\\n    delta_pp: 4.90\\\\n    p: 0.013\\\\n    b: 12\\\\n    c: 2\\\\n    seed: 42\\\\n\\\\n  replication:\\\\n    - {exp_id: exp-033, seed: 42, sc: 54.41, delta_pp: 4.90, p: 0.013, significant: true}\\\\n    - {exp_id: exp-052, seed: 123, sc: 53.9, delta_pp: 3.43, p: 0.039, significant: true}\\\\n    - {exp_id: exp-053, seed: 456, sc: 56.37, delta_pp: -0.49, p: 1.0, significant: false}\\\\n    # D060 correction: exp-052 p=0.039 (not 0.09). 2/3 significant at α=0.05.\\\\n\\\\n  oracle:\\\\n    - {exp_id: exp-031, dataset: FOLIO-204, oracle_acc: 89.71, sc: 75.49, delta_pp: 14.22, p: 2.0e-7}\\\\n    - {exp_id: exp-022, dataset: ProofWriter-600, oracle_acc: 86.67, sc: 75.17, delta_pp: 11.50, p: 9.21e-15}\\\\n\\\\n  type_c:\\\\n    exp_id: exp-046\\\\n    model: Mistral-7B\\\\n    dataset: ProofWriter-D5-600\\\\n    n: 600\\\\n    sc: 39.33\\\\n    sica: 36.50\\\\n    delta_pp: -2.83\\\\n    p: 0.0095\\\\n    note: \\\\\\\"FINAL numbers — do NOT use interim (n=303, Δ=-4.67pp)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  independence:\\\\n    mistral_folio_s123:\\\\n      fleiss_kappa: 0.412\\\\n      eff_k: 2.17\\\\n      source: \\\\\\\"comp-1 Worker verified (exp-052)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mistral_folio_s456:\\\\n      fleiss_kappa: 0.401\\\\n      eff_k: 2.22\\\\n      source: \\\\\\\"comp-1 Worker verified (exp-053)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mistral_folio_s42:\\\\n      fleiss_kappa: 0.500\\\\n      eff_k: 1.85\\\\n      source: \\\\\\\"Director-verified (exp-033)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    qwen14b_folio:\\\\n      fleiss_kappa: 0.744\\\\n      eff_k: 1.31\\\\n      unanimous_rate: 58.3\\\\n      source: \\\\\\\"comp-1 Worker verified (exp-026)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    qwen14b_logiqa:\\\\n      fleiss_kappa: 0.821\\\\n      eff_k: 1.20\\\\n      unanimous_rate: 63.0\\\\n      source: \\\\\\\"comp-1 Worker verified (exp-038)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mistral_folio_operational:\\\\n      unanimous_rate: 18.6\\\\n      override_precision: 70.6\\\\n      confirmation_bias: 31.9\\\\n      maxsat_sat_ratio: 0.961\\\\n      note: \\\\\\\"operational metrics from Director, retained for exp-033\\\\\\\"\\\\n    qwen14b_folio_operational:\\\\n      confirmation_bias: 62.3\\\\n      maxsat_sat_ratio: 0.991\\\\n      note: \\\\\\\"operational metrics from Director, retained\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mistral_pw600:\\\\n      fleiss_kappa: 0.210\\\\n      eff_k: 3.63\\\\n      source: \\\\\\\"Director-verified (exp-046)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    cross_seed_note: \\\\\\\"κ varies across seeds (0.50/0.41/0.40) but Δ non-monotonic with Eff-K (exp-033 Eff-K=1.85 has highest Δ=+4.90). Eff-K necessary not sufficient. exp-046 Eff-K=3.63 highest but SC=39% → negative Δ → need both sufficient Eff-K AND sufficient SC.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  k_sensitivity:\\\\n    note: \\\\\\\"D060 data; inverted-U curve\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data:\\\\n      - {k: 4, delta_pp: -1.47}\\\\n      - {k: 8, delta_pp: -0.98}\\\\n      - {k: 12, delta_pp: 4.90}\\\\n      - {k: 16, delta_pp: 1.47}\\\\n      - {k: 20, delta_pp: null, status: pending}\\\\n\\\\n  t_sensitivity:\\\\n    note: \\\\\\\"D060 data; effect fragility\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data:\\\\n      - {t: 0.7, delta_pp: 4.90, exp_id: exp-033}\\\\n      - {t: 1.0, delta_pp: 0.55, exp_id: exp-054}\\\\n\\\\n  remediation_failures:\\\\n    count: 9\\\\n    dimensions: 6\\\\n    strategies:\\\\n      - {name: \\\\\\\"Contrastive prompting\\\\\\\", dim: prompting, exp: exp-029, result: \\\\\\\"disc_rate 8.2%→6.0%, Δ=-1.1pp\\\\\\\"}\\\\n      - {name: \\\\\\\"Cross-model extraction\\\\\\\", dim: architecture, exp: exp-030, result: \\\\\\\"0% discriminative\\\\\\\"}\\\\n      - {name: \\\\\\\"Generational scaling (Qwen3)\\\\\\\", dim: capability, exp: exp-027, result: \\\\\\\"+0.49pp n.s.\\\\\\\"}\\\\n      - {name: \\\\\\\"Z3 feedback\\\\\\\", dim: verification, exp: exp-036, result: \\\\