{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017K3u5uywHX25KJGxo53UiC","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/analysis.tex:65:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/experiments.tex:96:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/introduction.tex:17:\\item We provide entropy-conditioned mechanism evidence: SICA gains concentrate in high-entropy problems ($+9.6$\\,pp, $n = 73$ for Mistral-7B), and the aggregate regime effect reflects the proportion of such problems in each model's trace distribution. Confirmation bias (62.3\\% vs.\\ 31.9\\%), override precision (28.6\\% vs.\\ 70.6\\%), and unanimous answer rate (58.8\\% vs.\\ 18.6\\%) quantify the causal path from model accuracy to constraint quality (\\S\\ref{sec:entropy})."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01APnYWuVJxCUteRUxQF13B3","session_id":"ff4131df-0538-40e9-a5d8-d0234a1df865","uuid":"cce8171c-d6d1-4d71-b802-22776d4f1e1e","timestamp":"2026-05-19T04:50:13.341Z"}
